    shapes: [["W bf16 [4096, 4096] (32 MB)", "INT4 + scales", "≈ 8 MB"]],
    code: "# speculative decoding (sketch)\ndraft = small.generate(ctx, k=4)\np_big = big.score(ctx + draft)            # one pass over k tokens\naccepted = accept_prefix(draft, p_small, p_big)",
    why: "Latency and cost per token decide whether a model is usable in production.",
    breaks: "Too aggressive quantization degrades quality, especially on reasoning and rare tokens; speculative decoding with a poor draft model gives no speedup.",
    trainInfer: "Mostly inference. FlashAttention is used in training too; quantization-aware training exists but post-training quantization is common.",
    security: "Downloaded quantized checkpoints are third-party artifacts (supply chain); quantization can change safety behaviour, so evals should be rerun on the deployed format.",
